      "content": "Their core logic is that if a measurable difference persists even after controlling for environmental factors like income or education, the remaining unexplained variance must be attributable to immutable biological differences. They argue that current environmental controls are insufficient or incomplete, thus leaving genetic inheritance as the most logical remaining variable to explain the observed discrepancy. Essentially, they frame the persistence of the gap as evidence of a fixed biological substrate rather than mere residual environmental influence. This reasoning posits that biological causation overrides environmental correlations in these specific instances.",
